# .agentignore
# Tells agentic IDEs not to read historical or sandbox directories, which prevents context
# collapse and hallucination. No tool reads this file natively:
# .agents/scripts/hyper_firewall.py renders it (gitignore syntax; `!` negations are skipped for
# Claude Code).
#
# What enforces it:
# - Claude Code: permissions.deny rules in .claude/settings.json.
# - Roo, Cursor, Windsurf, Antigravity: a managed block in their own ignore file, best-effort.
# None of this is a security boundary; `hyper_firewall.py render` prints the limits.
#
# Two sections: patterns above the `# Standard dev ignores` comment get Read and Edit denies, and
# patterns below it get Read denies. `.git/` stays root-anchored.

# Block the archive to prevent reading outdated drafts and Red Team reports
spec/archive/

# Block the sandbox to prevent reading unverified AI outputs
tests/candidate_outputs/

# Standard dev ignores
node_modules/
.env
__pycache__/
.git/

# BEGIN HACF MANAGED BLOCK: agentignore
# HACF: historical drafts and unverified outputs agents must not read (hyper_firewall.py).
spec/archive/
tests/candidate_outputs/
# END HACF MANAGED BLOCK: agentignore